# 6. HTTPS Check

### Command

```bash
curl -I https://google.com
```

### Output

```text
HTTP/2 301
location: https://www.google.com/
content-type: text/html; charset=UTF-8
server: gws
```

### Observation

The HTTPS request successfully reached Google and returned:

```text
HTTP/2 301
```

A `301` response indicates a permanent redirect from:

```text
https://google.com
```

to:

```text
https://www.google.com/
```

### Key Learning

A successful `curl` response confirms that DNS resolution, network connectivity, TCP/TLS communication, and the HTTP/HTTPS service path were working for this request.

