# Part 3 – Mini Task: Port Probe

## Step 1 – Identify a Listening Port

From `ss -tulpn`, I identified:

```text
Port: 22
Service: SSH
```

---

## Step 2 – Test the Port

### Command

```bash
nc -zv localhost 22
```

### Output

```text
Connection to localhost (127.0.0.1) 22 port [tcp/ssh] succeeded!
```

### Observation

The SSH port was reachable locally.

---

## Step 3 – Next Check

If the port is not reachable, I would check the service:

```bash
systemctl status <service>
```

Then verify the listening socket:

```bash
ss -tulpn
```

And check the firewall:

```bash
sudo ufw status
```

